          "text": "Joseph formally presents members of his family to Pharaoh as livestock keepers and secures their residence in Goshen. The chapter later returns to that settlement: while Egyptians accept service to Pharaoh after receiving food, Israel gains property in Goshen and increases greatly. These scenes place the family’s secure settlement alongside the wider crisis affecting the land.",
