          ],
          "text": "The famine is not a backdrop to the chapter but its driving condition: food has failed so severely that both Egypt and Canaan are described as languishing. This explains both the family’s request for pasture in Egypt and the Egyptians’ increasingly urgent exchanges for grain.",
