          ],
          "text": "The account traces a sequence of exchanges during the famine. Grain is first bought with money; after money is exhausted, livestock is exchanged for food; then the people offer their land and themselves to Pharaoh for food and seed. Joseph relocates the population to cities, provides seed for sowing, and establishes Pharaoh’s continuing one-fifth share of the harvest, while four parts remain for seed and household food. Priests are treated differently because they receive an allowance from Pharaoh and do not sell their land.",
