          "text": "Two personal scenes frame the public crisis. Jacob blesses Pharaoh, describes his 130 years as few and difficult in comparison with his ancestors, and later requires Joseph’s sworn promise not to bury him in Egypt but in the ancestral burial place. The hand-under-thigh gesture is joined in the passage to that solemn oath. The family’s allotted land is also called the land of Rameses; the chapter uses this as the place-name for their settlement.",
